<title>CANADA: CP Rail to buy C$260 mln of locomotives.</title>
<headline>CP Rail to buy C$260 mln of locomotives.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Pacific Railway, a unit of Canadian Pacific Ltd, said on Monday that it ordered 101 locomotives at a total cost of about C$260 million.</p>
<p>An order for 91 alternating current, 4,400 horsepower locomotives was placed with General Electric Transportation Systems, a unit of General Electric Co.</p>
<p>An additional order for 10 alternating current, 5,000 horsepower locomotives was placed with General Motors Diesel Division. The new locomotives are expected to be delivered during the last quarter of 1997 and in early 1998, Canadian Pacific said in a statement.</p>
</text>
